{
  "sn54.11:0.1": "Linked Discourses 54.11 ",
  "sn54.11:0.2": "Chapter Two ",
  "sn54.11:0.3": "Icchānaṅgala ",
  "sn54.11:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in a forest near Icchānaṅgala. ",
  "sn54.11:1.2": "There he addressed the mendicants, ",
  "sn54.11:1.3": "“Mendicants, I wish to go on retreat for three months. ",
  "sn54.11:1.4": "No-one should approach me, except the one who brings my almsfood.” ",
  "sn54.11:1.5": "“Yes, sir,” replied those mendicants. And no-one approached him, except the one who brought the almsfood. ",
  "sn54.11:2.1": "Then after three months had passed, the Buddha came out of retreat and addressed the mendicants: ",
  "sn54.11:2.2": "“Mendicants, if wanderers who follow another religion were to ask you: ",
  "sn54.11:2.3": "‘Reverends, what was the ascetic Gotama’s usual meditation during the rainy season residence?’ You should answer them like this. ",
  "sn54.11:2.4": "‘Reverends, the ascetic Gotama’s usual meditation during the rainy season residence was immersion due to mindfulness of breathing.’ ",
  "sn54.11:2.5": "In this regard: mindful, I breathe in. Mindful, I breathe out. ",
  "sn54.11:2.6": "Breathing in heavily I know: ‘I’m breathing in heavily.’ Breathing out heavily I know: ‘I’m breathing out heavily.’ ",
  "sn54.11:2.7": "Breathing in lightly I know: ‘I’m breathing in lightly.’ Breathing out lightly I know: ‘I’m breathing out lightly.’ ",
  "sn54.11:2.8": "I know: ‘I’ll breathe in experiencing the w